cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its records, please cite it as below, together with the SOFTENG 2026 paper that defines the framework."
title: "5LTEP-L5: 5L-TEP Layer 5 Governance and Publication (Recife instance)"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of Layer 5 (Governance and Publication) of the
  Five-Layer Trust Engineering Pyramid (5L-TEP, SOFTENG 2026) for open
  government data on CKAN portals. Every day it reads the public summaries of
  Layers 1-4 and, per dataset, shows how far each layer reaches, the global
  quality score of the paper where the four layers meet, an interval where they
  do not, an integrity factor for undocumented metadata changes, and what can
  already be checked. It informs and never decides: each dataset has a
  printable, citable record identified by the SHA-256 of its content, quality
  measurements are published in W3C DQV with PROV provenance, and the outcome
  after a report is only observed. Three files (portal, sources, policy) adapt
  it to another portal.
